  "query_preview": "(Thanksgiving through Sunday)...\n\nThanksgiving and Friday will be dry and warmer with northeast \nwinds gusting to 35 mph along and below the coastal slopes of the \nmountains. High temperatures on Thanksgiving will warm around 5\ndegrees for the deserts onto the desert slopes of the mountains\nand 5 to 10 degrees from the coastal slopes of the mountains to\nthe coast with warmest high temperatures in the lower 80s for the\nlower deserts and for inland coastal areas into the western\nvalleys.\n\nThere will be additional warming on Friday of a few to around 5\ndegrees with warmest high temperatures on Friday in the lower to\nmid 80s for the lower deserts and for inland coastal areas into\nthe western valleys.\n\nOnshore flow will return for Saturday into next week. High\ntemperatures for the coast and valleys will cool around 5 degrees\non Saturday from the coast to the mountains. There will be\nadditional cooling of high temperatures on Sunday of around 5\ndegrees near the coast to 5 to 10 degrees for the mountains. \nHigh temperatures on Sunday will range from the mid to upper 60s\nfor the far inland valleys to the lower 70s for the coast into the\nwestern valleys.\n\nThe next chance for precipitation will be for late Sunday into\nMonday with the chance for measurable precipitation from the coast\nto the mountains around 50 percent and the chance for 0.5 inch or\nmore of rainfall ranging from 10 to 15 percent near the coast to\naround 25 percent for the mountains",
